# ── RackTrack client production build config ──────────────────────────
# Copy to `client/.env.production` and set the PUBLIC backend URL.
#
# IMPORTANT: leave EMPTY to use same-origin (recommended when the client is
# served by / proxied through the API host or a tunnel — requests go to the
# same origin the app was loaded from). Only set an absolute URL when the API
# lives on a DIFFERENT public host — and it MUST be https:// (iOS ATS /
# Android cleartext policy block plain http, and http://localhost is the
# phone itself on a real device).
VITE_API_BASE=
# e.g. VITE_API_BASE=https://api.racktrack.example.com

# ── Default switch address (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# Pre-fills the switch host on the live-switch pages and gives the port probe a
# last-resort candidate when the server remembers no previous host.
#
# LEAVE EMPTY on any deployment without a route to that switch — notably the
# public demo. This was hardcoded to an office address, so the demo probed a
# host that could not exist there and then displayed that private IP on screen
# as the switch's management address. Empty means "ask the server, then the
# user", which is the honest default.
VITE_FALLBACK_SWITCH_HOST=
# In the office, e.g. VITE_FALLBACK_SWITCH_HOST=192.168.1.33
